    fix: drop hidden-state cache requirement from completeness reconciliation
    
    Ruling on the long-uncommitted hunk (audit lever H13, rigor_audit/00 §C):
    KEEP. hidden_states/ caches are .gitignored and absent from every cell
    on this machine, so the committed semantics (complete = full step rows
    AND a hidden-state .npz) would mark every already-complete run
    incomplete on any resume and trigger mass re-collection. Module 0
    verified no on-disk output was ever produced under the edited
    semantics, so history is unaffected; this changes future resumes only.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

